# Flare .gitignore
# Root safety net. Each app in apps/ also has its own .gitignore from its template;
# the stack sections below repeat the important rules so nothing slips through.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, do not add broad patterns for these:
#   - simulated seed data and the labelled RO/EN test set (*.json, *.csv, ...)
#   - .env.example
#   - lockfiles
# Ignoring does not protect files that are already tracked or already in history.
# If a secret is ever committed, rotate it.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# --- Personal Claude Code config (the shared .claude/settings.json IS committed) ---
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Real passenger data: never commit (demo uses simulated data only) ---
uploads/
photos/

# --- Local databases and logs ---
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log

# --- Demo fallback recording (large; share outside git) ---
/recordings/

# --- Temp and scratch ---
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.swp

# --- OS and editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Node (flare-webapp, flare-mobile, scripts) ---
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# --- Vite ---
.vite/

# --- Expo (managed workflow: no native folders) ---
.expo/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*
/apps/flare-mobile/ios/
/apps/flare-mobile/android/
*.jks
*.p8
*.mobileprovision

# --- Maven / Java ---
apps/flare-backend/target/
*.class
hs_err_pid*

# --- IDEs ---
*.iml
.classpath
.project
.settings/

# --- Design exploration screenshots (regenerate with docs/design/explorations/render.mjs) ---
docs/design/explorations/shots/
docs/design/reference/shots/
